<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick III, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1597">1597</a>–<a href="/years/1659">1659</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick III, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp, ruled from 1616 to 1659 and kept a cultured Lutheran court at Gottorp. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrichstadt">Friedrichstadt</a> in 1621 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Remonstrant refugees and sent the embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-olearius">Adam Olearius</a>. Allying with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, he won full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> for his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> lands in 1658.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-duke-of-holstein-gottorp.jpg" alt="Frederick III, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to David Klöcker Ehrenstrahl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frederick_III,_Duke_of_Holstein-Gottorp_by_David_Kl%C3%B6cker_Ehrenstrahl_(crop).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
